############################################################
# First attempt at the same control, kept because it is a second
# ve=0 failure and because it is why the harness was rebuilt.
#
# mpv vanished at ~250 s. The kernel survived. It printed no
# 'Exiting...' line, which mpv emits on every ordinary termination
# including errors, and there was no OOM kill and no coredump -- so it
# died on a signal. WHICH signal was not recoverable: this rootfs has
# /proc/sys/debug/exception-trace = 0, so the kernel prints nothing for
# a userspace fault. dmesg being empty was therefore not evidence.
# The script now sets exception-trace=1, captures mpv's exit status via
# wait(), and restarts mpv so one death no longer ends the run.
############################################################
